{
  "version": 1,
  "_notes": [
    "Shared TS/Rust parity vectors for the typed scalar expression evaluator (Task 16 TS, Task 18 Rust).",
    "Each vector's `ast` is an already-typed TypedScalarExpression tree with source spans omitted (the evaluator never reads them); a test-only loader fills dummy {start:0,end:0} spans on decode.",
    "`bindings` maps bindingId -> a JSON-encoded ScalarEvaluation, used to build a mock environment.lookupBinding.",
    "`tripwireBindingIds` names bindingIds that must never be looked up in this vector (short-circuit proof); a conforming implementation must not call lookupBinding for them.",
    "Convention: when a node's static `type` is null, the runtime ScalarEvaluation.type placeholder is always {kind:\"number\"} (mirrors expressionTypecheck.ts's existing unknown-type default) - Rust must match this exact placeholder for vector parity to hold.",
    "Convention: for binary operators other than && and ||, both operands are evaluated unconditionally; if both error, the LEFT operand's error wins.",
    "eager-arithmetic-both-error-left-wins (added for Task 18, the Rust evaluator) exercises the left-error-wins convention above for the first time - no prior vector covered it, only the short-circuit && / || vectors exercised a single-sided error."
  ],
